    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0105" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">PPS Files, Lot 64 D 563</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State for
                        Public Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barrett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Webb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1951-06-06">June 6, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A member of my staff has prepared this memorandum on American public opinion,
                    which I think will be of interest to you.</p>
                <p>This memorandum will particularly concern those who will be the members of the
                    “staff group” mentioned in recommendation “<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>” of
                    Mr. Lay’s Memorandum to the NSC of June 1.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d22-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Barrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d22-a1.xml" xpointer="d22-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
